{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":42.529998779296875,"text":"In the heart of the city, at the spot where people in Heraklion say, meet me at the lions, there is a fountain finished in 1628. The city owes it to Francesco Moricini, who solved a problem decades old. Heraklion did not have enough drinking water. He built an aqueduct that brought water down from Mount Juctus, about 15 kilometers away, using the slope of the ground alone and no pump at all. The basin has eight lobes carved with sea creatures, dolphins, and nymphs, and the four lions holding it up are some 300 years older than the fountain. They were not made for it. They were brought from somewhere else and reused. Water still comes out of their mouths today.","words":[{"word":"In","start":0,"end":0.5400000214576721},{"word":"the","start":0.5400000214576721,"end":0.7400000095367432},{"word":"heart","start":0.7400000095367432,"end":0.8999999761581421},{"word":"of","start":0.8999999761581421,"end":1.2400000095367432},{"word":"the","start":1.2400000095367432,"end":1.2400000095367432},{"word":"city","start":1.2400000095367432,"end":1.4600000381469727},{"word":"at","start":1.7799999713897705,"end":1.899999976158142},{"word":"the","start":1.899999976158142,"end":2.119999885559082},{"word":"spot","start":2.119999885559082,"end":2.319999933242798},{"word":"where","start":2.319999933242798,"end":2.559999942779541},{"word":"people","start":2.559999942779541,"end":2.859999895095825},{"word":"in","start":2.859999895095825,"end":3.200000047683716},{"word":"Heraklion","start":3.200000047683716,"end":3.4200000762939453},{"word":"say","start":3.4200000762939453,"end":3.940000057220459},{"word":"meet","start":4.380000114440918,"end":4.380000114440918},{"word":"me","start":4.380000114440918,"end":4.539999961853027},{"word":"at","start":4.539999961853027,"end":4.639999866485596},{"word":"the","start":4.639999866485596,"end":4.940000057220459},{"word":"lions","start":4.940000057220459,"end":5.2199997901916